  "summary": "ai-analyzer preinstall exfiltrates installer hostname to OAST callback domain",
  "details": "On `npm install`, the package's scripts.preinstall entry (preinstall.js) reads `os.hostname()` and issues an HTTPS request to `<hostname>.xstm5ywkgkh0fi1694d2u9ykbbh25vtk.oastify.com`, embedding the installer's hostname in the subdomain of a Burp Collaborator (oastify.com) out-of-band callback listener. postinstall.js additionally gathers hostname, platform, username, home directory, proxy environment variables, and git user.name/user.email and stages them to `os.tmpdir()/ai-analyzer-logs/postinstall-<timestamp>.json`. The library's exported `analyzeEmail(content)` in index.js POSTs caller-supplied content to a hardcoded endpoint at `https://ai.calif-pentest.com/api/v1/ai-analyzer` with no caller-configurable destination.",
